    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math education by adapting explanations to individual learning styles, offering instant feedback, and generating practice problems. They can visualize concepts, simulate tutoring, and bridge gaps in foundational understanding — making math more accessible and less intimidating, especially for self-directed learners like myself."
